<header class="hero">
  <div class="overlay">
    <h1>The Count of Saint Germain</h1>
    <p class="tagline">
      Gather close, good folk—where stories dance, laughter lingers, and a touch of indulgence
      is the noblest of virtues
    </p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section">
  <h2>The Welcome</h2>
  <p>
    Welcome, travelers! I am the Count of Saint Germain—teller of tales, purveyor of finery,
    and a humble servant to mirth and mischief alike. Step lightly, speak freely,
    and let your heart catch a little delight along the way.
  </p>

  <p>
    Crowns fit for kings and knaves, blades for daring souls, capes to make the wind sing,
    and adornments to provoke admiration and a chuckle or two—all offered
    with a story, a smile, and just enough flourish to make even Sir John Falstaff pause.
  </p>

  <p>
    Life is meant to be tasted, toasted, and occasionally toasted again.
    Moderation, they say, is virtue—but who among us remembers virtue in a moment of revelry?
  </p>
</section>

<section class="section light">
  <h2>Wares & Wonders</h2>
  <p>
    Look freely, try boldly, and laugh often. Courage, wit, and a fine hat all walk hand in hand,
    and here, you may have them together.
  </p>
  <ul class="wares">
    <li>Handcrafted Crowns & Circlets</li>
    <li>Wooden Swords & Shields</li>
    <li>Capes & Costume Accessories</li>
    <li>Earrings & Jewelry</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Appearances & Bookings</h2>
  <p>
    The Count of Saint Germain appears at festivals, gatherings, and celebrations of all kinds.
    By day, nimble and family-friendly; by lantern-light, roguish and mischievous,
    always with charm, story, and a well-timed wink.
  </p>
</section>

